WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.575
When artificial intelligence makes a
decision,

2
00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:04.850
we often ask: why?

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.125
Explainable AI gives us clues,

4
00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:09.140
such as highlights on a picture.

5
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.450
But an explanation can look convincing

6
00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:14.100
and still mislead us.

7
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.375
Highlighting the bird looks sensible.

8
00:00:16.425 --> 00:00:19.025
Does it reflect what the model actually
used?

9
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.900
From three hundred sixty-two publications,

10
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.250
the authors organized evaluation methods
into forty-one groups:

11
00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:29.225
a map for choosing tests.

12
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.750
The framework asks:

13
00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:33.825
what kind of explanation do you have?

14
00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:35.350
Which qualities matter?

15
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:38.650
And how does a test use or change the
model and data?

16
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.925
Fidelity asks whether an explanation
reflects the model.

17
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.975
Simplicity asks whether it stays concise.

18
00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:49.675
Different tests reveal different
qualities.

19
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.425
Combine complementary tests.

20
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.675
This is a review and framework.

21
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.075
Automated scores alone cannot tell us

22
00:00:57.125 --> 00:00:59.650
whether people understand an explanation.

23
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.725
Now let's use the companion website.

24
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.700
Open the address on screen,

25
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.550
scroll to Metrics Overview,

26
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.240
and click Filter to reveal the options.

27
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.775
For a picture heatmap, choose F A,

28
00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:14.825
meaning feature attributions.

29
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:17.200
Under Desiderata, choose Fidelity:

30
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.685
does the explanation reflect the model?

31
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.040
Next, choose contextuality level three:

32
00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.715
changing inputs and observing the model.

33
00:01:25.815 --> 00:01:29.740
Here, the filters narrow forty-one groups
to three candidates.

34
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.500
Click Guided Perturbation Fidelity.

35
00:01:32.575 --> 00:01:35.875
Read the approaches, variations, and
references.

36
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.900
Helper Functions explains choices

37
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.675
such as how to change inputs.

38
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.875
Hide highlighted image regions, then
observe the prediction.

39
00:01:43.925 --> 00:01:46.075
Compare against random masking.

40
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.175
This gives evidence of faithfulness,

41
00:01:48.225 --> 00:01:49.700
not automatic proof.

42
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.075
Use the site to choose tests,

43
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:53.900
then run them in your workflow.

44
00:01:53.975 --> 00:01:56.450
Ask how the explanation was tested.
